# K02c: the caller's merge result reaches read THROUGH an intermediate caller that binds no `copy` of its own -- mid
# inherits read's hidden input and forwards what it received (the book §12: an inherited input before the lexical
# fallback).  caller's copy (22) wins over the unit's (1).  Success is 7.
Model: (int: value 1)
Other: (int: value 22)
copy: merge: Model
fn: read () int
return: copy\value
fn: mid () int
return: read()
fn: caller () int
    copy: merge: Other
    return: mid()
end: caller
int: result caller()
if: result != 22
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
